
=== FreeJ API

=== Current native source map

src/Makefile.am groups the engine, media, controllers, displays and JS
bindings. Context::cafudda in src/context.cpp drives the frame step in
src/engine/. The CLI in src/freej.cpp and Qt in qt/qfreej.cpp assemble
the native frontends. Start a JS entry-point search in src/jsparser.cpp.
See INSTALL for the profile build, adapter rebuild and installed client.

* Movie layer. The Context constructor calls init_factory, which calls
  freej_media::register_movie_layer in src/video_layer.cpp for
  MovieLayer/ffmpeg. src/video_layer_js.cpp is the
  JS binding. Start decoder changes in src/media/movie_decoder.cpp, the
  only member of the private libmovie_decoder target that uses FFmpeg
  headers. The layer worker calls VideoLayer::feed and borrows its playback
  pixels until the next feed or close. The worker copies the finished
  frame into the layer store, and the compositor holds a frame lease
  while blitting. Open and close stop the worker before replacing decoder
  storage. The explicit registration call keeps the adapter reachable
  when linking archives. movie-replay-test checks decoding, end-of-stream
  drain, seek, reopen and resampling against tests/show-replay/movie-av.mov.

* OSC controller. src/osc_ctrl.cpp registers OscController/core with
  FACTORY_REGISTER_INSTANTIATOR. The JS class is registered in
  src/jsparser.cpp. The liblo receiver copies its borrowed route and
  arguments before returning. OscController::poll drains the owned queue
  on the engine thread that owns JS. Keep JS values and calls on that
  thread. The static package retains the factory initializer with
  --whole-archive. tests/show-replay/replay.py --case osc uses loopback
  callbacks, stop/restart, self-removal and reset fixtures.

* Brightness effect. Context::init calls Plugger::refresh in src/plugger.cpp.
  Compatibility discovers the module in plugin directories. Static uses
  the built-in descriptor in the pinned frei0r archive. Both create the
  Freior factory in src/frei0r.cpp, which owns parameter and instance
  callbacks. The layer worker processes its ordered effects. The plugin
  borrows the input and the instance-owned output during each call.
  The prototype and module stay alive until the last instance is released.
  The static link retains the factory initializer and resolves the bundle
  descriptor registry through the SDK archive group. The compatibility
  test-effects.py and static frei0r-host-test exercise this host.
  tests/native-ci-run.sh records the shared 24-frame fixture in each profile.

